# Frontend layout

Fill leftover space with a flex/grid chain. Never size panes with `100vh` minus a guessed header height.

- `html/body/#root` are `height: 100%`. The app shell is `height: 100dvh` and `overflow: hidden`.
- Every nested flex/grid child that should shrink uses `min-width: 0` and `min-height: 0`.
- Side-by-side panes: `grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr)`.
- Measure a dedicated inner probe (`width: 100%`), not a padded scroller. Pass that width into `react-pdf` `Page`.
- Use `ResizeObserver` + `requestAnimationFrame`. Skip state updates when the integer size did not change.
- Do not stretch the PDF canvas with CSS `width: 100%` — that desyncs the text layer.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="pane-body" ref={ref}>
  <Page width={Math.floor(entry.contentRect.width - 8)} />
</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="pane-body">
  <div className="pdf-width-probe" ref={probeRef} />
  {width > 0 ? <Page width={width} /> : null}
</div>
```
